  "narrative": "The new robustness analyses consistently reinforce the central measured association: feature_027=1 versus feature_027=0 is associated with much higher outcome_014 in the supplied dataset. In every valid stratum (H241-H251), the signed mean difference is approximately +0.78 to +0.81 and the 95% lower bound remains above +0.74. These differences are orders of magnitude larger than any plausible 10% clinical scale for outcome_014 and far above the earlier accepted reference effect of about +0.80. The complete-case-like H241 result also suggests the association is not an artifact of the missingness patterns targeted by the eligibility constraints; middle age (H242), high and low observed clinical-value strata for feature_056/feature_016/feature_053 (H243-H248), and large categorical strata (H249-H251) all show essentially the same enormous positive contrast. Therefore I accept H241-H251 as evidence of a highly robust dataset-specific measured association and close them. I close H252 as unresolved because the eligibility specification produced an invalid comparison cell (3 vs 23 observations, insufficient cell n), so it provides neither confirmation nor disconfirmation. No new secondary association is supported by these results. The multiplicity of stratum tests is not a credible explanation for the effect, given its size, prior validation of the central feature_027-outcome_014 association, and coherence across strata. The most likely interpretation is that feature_027 is label-like, technical, batch-related, deterministic, or otherwise leakage/confounding-prone in this dataset, not evidence of causal biology or external generalizability. No validation is requested because voluntary validation budget is exhausted and the claim set does not require it.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 19 appraise final robustness sweep complete. H241-H251 accepted and closed: feature_027=1 vs 0 associated with outcome_014 increases ~+0.78 to +0.81 in valid complete-case, age-band, clinical-median, and categorical strata; lower bounds > +0.74. H252 closed unresolved due invalid insufficient cell_n (3 vs 23). Central conclusion now: extremely strong, validated, dataset-specific measured association between feature_027 and outcome_014, plausibly leakage/label-like/technical, not causal or generalizable. Secondary outcome/predictor lines remain unsupported/closed. No validation requests remain; stop further exploration unless new independent evidence appears."
